IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`
IMPORT `snap3-logic`

-- SECTION 2022, DISPOSITION OF CLAIMS (7 U.S.C. 2022), lines 1796-1857 of usc07-ch51.txt.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. A function answers MAYBE BOOLEAN (or MAYBE NUMBER, MAYBE DATE) with: JUST TRUE = the text says yes;
-- JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words; NOTHING = the text does not say. Money is a NUMBER of dollars.
-- The Secretary's judgments ("determines", "to the satisfaction of the Secretary") are conditional inputs, never guessed.
-- Source is a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text.

DECLARE `s 2022(b)(1) means of collection` IS ONE OF
    `s 2022(b)(1)(A) reducing the allotment of the household`
    `s 2022(b)(1)(B) withholding amounts from unemployment compensation from a member of the household under subsection (c)`
    `s 2022(b)(1)(C) recovering from Federal pay or a Federal income tax refund under subsection (d)`
    `s 2022(b)(1)(D) any other means`

DECLARE `s 2022(d) source of recovery` IS ONE OF
    `s 2022(d) Federal pay (including salaries and pensions)`
    `s 2022(d) a Federal income tax refund`
    `s 2022(d) any other source`

§ `s 2022 -- disposition of claims`

§§ `s 2022(a) general authority of the Secretary`

-- src:1799 | Except in the case of an at-risk amount required under section 2025(c)(1)(D)(i)(II) of this title or the payment or disposition of a State share under section 2013(a)(2) of this title, the Secretary shall have the power to determine the amount of and settle and adjust any claim and to compromise or deny all or part of any such claim or claims arising under the provisions of this chapter or the regulations issued pursuant to this chapter, including, but not limited to, claims arising from fraudulent and nonfraudulent overissuances to recipients, including the power to waive claims if the Secretary determines that to do so would serve the purposes of this chapter.
@ref s 2022(a)(1) the Secretary's power to determine, settle, adjust, compromise, deny and waive claims (src:1799)
-- In plain words: the Secretary can fix the amount of a claim arising under the chapter (including a claim for a fraudulent or non-fraudulent overissuance to a recipient), settle or adjust it, compromise or deny
-- all or part of it, and waive it if that would serve the chapter's purposes. Two things are outside this power: an at-risk amount under section 2025(c)(1)(D)(i)(II) and a State share under section 2013(a)(2).
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Kind of decision`
      `the claim is an at-risk amount required under section 2025(c)(1)(D)(i)(II) or the payment or disposition of a State share under section 2013(a)(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary determines that waiving the claim would serve the purposes of this chapter` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2022(a)(1) the Secretary has the power to make the decision about the claim` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the claim is an at-risk amount required under section 2025(c)(1)(D)(i)(II) or the payment or disposition of a State share under section 2013(a)(2)` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except in the case of an at-risk amount required under section 2025(c)(1)(D)(i)(II) of this title or the payment or disposition of a State share under section 2013(a)(2) of this title"
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the decision` EQUALS `grant a waiver` THEN
            -- the waiver is a power "if the Secretary determines that to do so would serve the purposes of this chapter": the determination is the input
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Secretary determines that to do so would serve the purposes of this chapter"
            -- note (a failed "if"; see NOTES.md, Marginal readings)
            `the Secretary determines that waiving the claim would serve the purposes of this chapter`
        IF `the decision` EQUALS `establish a claim for an overissuance` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to determine the amount of and settle and adjust any claim and to compromise or deny all or part of any such claim or claims"
            NOTHING

-- src:1799 | Such powers with respect to claims against recipients may be delegated by the Secretary to State agencies.
@ref s 2022(a)(1) delegation to State agencies of the powers over claims against recipients (src:1799)
GIVEN `the claim is against a recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2022(a)(1) the Secretary may delegate the powers over the claim to State agencies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the claim is against a recipient` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Such powers with respect to claims against recipients may be delegated"
            NOTHING

-- src:1799 | The Secretary shall have the power to reduce amounts otherwise due to a State agency under section 2025 of this title to collect unpaid claims assessed against the State agency if the State agency has declined or exhausted its appeal rights under section 2023 of this title.
@ref s 2022(a)(1) reducing amounts due to a State agency to collect unpaid claims against it (src:1799)
-- In plain words: if a State agency has not appealed an assessed claim, or has used up its appeal rights under section 2023, the Secretary may collect the claim by reducing what is otherwise due to it under section 2025.
GIVEN `the claim is an unpaid claim assessed against the State agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency has declined or exhausted its appeal rights under section 2023` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2022(a)(1) the Secretary may reduce amounts otherwise due to the State agency under section 2025 to collect the claim` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the claim is an unpaid claim assessed against the State agency` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to collect unpaid claims assessed against the State agency"
            NOTHING
        IF `the State agency has declined or exhausted its appeal rights under section 2023` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the State agency has declined or exhausted its appeal rights under section 2023 of this title"
            -- note (a failed "if"; see NOTES.md, Marginal readings)
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1801 | To the extent that a State agency does not pay a claim established under section 2025(c)(1) of this title, including an agreement to have all or part of the claim paid through a reduction in Federal administrative funding, within 30 days from the date on which the bill for collection is received by the State agency, the State agency shall be liable for interest on any unpaid portion of such claim accruing from the date on which the bill for collection was received by the State agency, unless the State agency appeals the claim under section 2025(c)(7) of this title.
@ref s 2022(a)(2) the State agency is liable for interest on a quality control claim it does not pay in 30 days (src:1801)
-- In plain words: a State agency that does not pay (or agree to pay by a cut in its Federal administrative funding) a claim under section 2025(c)(1) within 30 days of receiving the bill owes interest on the unpaid part,
-- unless it appeals the claim under section 2025(c)(7); an appealed claim has its own start date for interest (the next function).
GIVEN `the claim is one established under section 2025(c)(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency paid the claim, or agreed to pay it through a reduction in Federal administrative funding, within 30 days from the date on which the bill for collection was received` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency appeals the claim under section 2025(c)(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2022(a)(2) the State agency is liable for interest on the unpaid portion of the claim` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the claim is one established under section 2025(c)(1)` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a claim established under section 2025(c)(1) of this title"
            NOTHING
        IF `the State agency paid the claim, or agreed to pay it through a reduction in Federal administrative funding, within 30 days from the date on which the bill for collection was received` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "To the extent that a State agency does not pay a claim"
            -- note (a failed condition; see NOTES.md, Marginal readings)
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the State agency appeals the claim under section 2025(c)(7)` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the State agency appeals the claim under section 2025(c)(7) of this title"
            -- note (liability under this sentence; the second sentence gives an appealed claim its own start date)
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1801 | If the State agency appeals such claim (in whole or in part), the interest on any unpaid portion of the claim shall accrue from the date of the decision on the administrative appeal, or from a date that is 1 year after the date the bill is received, whichever is earlier, until the date the unpaid portion of the payment is received.
@ref s 2022(a)(2) the date from which interest accrues on an unpaid claim (src:1801)
-- In plain words: with no appeal, interest runs from the day the bill was received. With an appeal, from the earlier of the day of the decision on the administrative appeal and one year after the bill was received.
-- If the State agency paid the claim within 30 days there is no unpaid portion, and so no date.
GIVEN `the claim is one established under section 2025(c)(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency paid the claim, or agreed to pay it through a reduction in Federal administrative funding, within 30 days from the date on which the bill for collection was received` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency appeals the claim (in whole or in part)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the bill for collection was received by the State agency` IS A DATE
      `the date of the decision on the administrative appeal, if there has been one` IS A MAYBE DATE
-- "1 year after the date the bill is received": a bill received on 29 February has no anniversary a year later; `add years` clamps to 28 February (assumed, not ruled; NOTES.md, fork F-2022-1).
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 2022(a)(2) the date from which interest on the unpaid portion accrues` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the claim is one established under section 2025(c)(1)` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a claim established under section 2025(c)(1) of this title"
            NOTHING
        IF `the State agency paid the claim, or agreed to pay it through a reduction in Federal administrative funding, within 30 days from the date on which the bill for collection was received` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the interest on any unpaid portion of the claim shall accrue"
            -- note (there is no unpaid portion)
            NOTHING
        IF NOT `the State agency appeals the claim (in whole or in part)` THEN JUST `the date on which the bill for collection was received by the State agency`
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the date of the decision on the administrative appeal, if there has been one`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (`add years` `the date on which the bill for collection was received by the State agency` 1)
                WHEN JUST decided THEN
                    IF Day decided AT MOST Day (`add years` `the date on which the bill for collection was received by the State agency` 1)
                    THEN JUST decided
                    ELSE JUST (`add years` `the date on which the bill for collection was received by the State agency` 1)

-- src:1801 | If the State agency pays such claim (in whole or in part, including an agreement to have all or part of the claim paid through a reduction in Federal administrative funding) and the claim is subsequently overturned through administrative or judicial appeal, any amounts paid by the State agency shall be promptly returned with interest, accruing from the date the payment is received until the date the payment is returned.
@ref s 2022(a)(2) amounts paid on a claim later overturned are returned with interest (src:1801)
GIVEN `the State agency paid the claim in whole or in part, including through an agreement to have all or part of the claim paid through a reduction in Federal administrative funding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim was subsequently overturned through administrative or judicial appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2022(a)(2) the amounts paid by the State agency must be promptly returned with interest` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency paid the claim in whole or in part, including through an agreement to have all or part of the claim paid through a reduction in Federal administrative funding` AND `the claim was subsequently overturned through administrative or judicial appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the claim is subsequently overturned through administrative or judicial appeal"
            NOTHING

-- src:1802 | (3) Computation of interest
-- src:1803 | Any interest assessed under this paragraph shall be computed at a rate determined by the Secretary based on the average of the bond equivalent of the weekly 90-day Treasury bill auction rates during the period such interest accrues.
@ref s 2022(a)(3) the rate at which interest is computed (src:1802-1803)
-- In plain words: the rate is the one the Secretary determines, based on the average of the weekly 90-day Treasury bill auction rates (bond equivalent) over the period the interest accrues. The rate is the Secretary's: an input.
GIVEN `the rate determined by the Secretary` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2022(a)(3) the rate at which interest is computed` MEANS
    `the rate determined by the Secretary`

-- src:1802 | (3) Computation of interest
-- src:1803 | Any interest assessed under this paragraph shall be computed at a rate determined by the Secretary based on the average of the bond equivalent of the weekly 90-day Treasury bill auction rates during the period such interest accrues.
@ref s 2022(a)(3) the average of the weekly rates on which the Secretary's rate is based (src:1802-1803)
-- The text says the rate is "based on" this average; it does not say the rate equals it, and it does not give the day-count basis for the interest amount (NOTES.md, fork F-2022-2).
GIVEN `the bond equivalent of the weekly 90-day Treasury bill auction rates during the period such interest accrues` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2022(a)(3) the average of the weekly 90-day Treasury bill auction rates` MEANS
    IF null `the bond equivalent of the weekly 90-day Treasury bill auction rates during the period such interest accrues`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (sum `the bond equivalent of the weekly 90-day Treasury bill auction rates during the period such interest accrues` DIVIDED BY count `the bond equivalent of the weekly 90-day Treasury bill auction rates during the period such interest accrues`)

-- src:1804 | (4) Joint and several liability of household members
-- src:1805 | Each adult member of a household shall be jointly and severally liable for the value of any overissuance of benefits.
@ref s 2022(a)(4) joint and several liability of the adult members of a household (src:1804-1805)
-- In plain words: every adult member of a household is liable, jointly and severally, for the whole value of an overissuance of benefits to the household.
GIVEN `s 2012(m) the individual or group is a household` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the member is an adult` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2022(a)(4) the member is jointly and severally liable for the value of the overissuance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the member is an adult` AND `s 2012(m) the individual or group is a household` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Each adult member of a household"
            NOTHING

§§ `s 2022(b) collection of overissuances`

-- src:1806 | (b) Collection of overissuances
-- src:1807 | (1) In general
-- src:1808 | Except as otherwise provided in this subsection, a State agency shall collect any overissuance of benefits issued to a household by—
-- src:1809 | (A) reducing the allotment of the household;
-- src:1810 | (B) withholding amounts from unemployment compensation from a member of the household under subsection (c);
-- src:1811 | (C) recovering from Federal pay or a Federal income tax refund under subsection (d); or
-- src:1812 | (D) any other means.
@ref s 2022(b)(1) the State agency shall collect an overissuance (src:1806-1812)
-- In plain words: unless paragraph (2) lifts it, a State agency must collect any overissuance of benefits to a household, by cutting the allotment, withholding unemployment compensation, recovering from Federal pay or a Federal tax refund, or any other means.
GIVEN `an overissuance of benefits was issued to the household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (2) says paragraph (1) does not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2022(b)(1) the State agency must collect the overissuance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an overissuance of benefits was issued to the household` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any overissuance of benefits issued to a household"
            NOTHING
        IF `paragraph (2) says paragraph (1) does not apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except as otherwise provided in this subsection"
            JUST FALSE
        IF `paragraph (2) says paragraph (1) does not apply` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the State agency has demonstrated cost-ineffectiveness to the Secretary's satisfaction is the Secretary's judgment
            NOTHING

-- src:1806 | (b) Collection of overissuances
-- src:1807 | (1) In general
-- src:1808 | Except as otherwise provided in this subsection, a State agency shall collect any overissuance of benefits issued to a household by—
-- src:1809 | (A) reducing the allotment of the household;
-- src:1810 | (B) withholding amounts from unemployment compensation from a member of the household under subsection (c);
-- src:1811 | (C) recovering from Federal pay or a Federal income tax refund under subsection (d); or
-- src:1812 | (D) any other means.
@ref s 2022(b)(1) the means by which a State agency collects (src:1806-1812)
GIVEN `the means` IS A `s 2022(b)(1) means of collection`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2022(b)(1) the State agency may collect the overissuance by the means` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the means`
        WHEN `s 2022(b)(1)(A) reducing the allotment of the household` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 2022(b)(1)(B) withholding amounts from unemployment compensation from a member of the household under subsection (c)` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 2022(b)(1)(C) recovering from Federal pay or a Federal income tax refund under subsection (d)` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 2022(b)(1)(D) any other means` THEN JUST TRUE

-- src:1813 | (2) Cost effectiveness
-- src:1814 | Paragraph (1) shall not apply if the State agency demonstrates to the satisfaction of the Secretary that all of the means referred to in paragraph (1) are not cost effective.
@ref s 2022(b)(2) paragraph (1) does not apply if collecting by every means is not cost effective (src:1813-1814)
-- In plain words: a State agency need not collect if it shows the Secretary that every means in paragraph (1) is not cost effective. Whether it has shown it "to the satisfaction of the Secretary" is the Secretary's judgment: an input.
GIVEN `the State agency has demonstrated to the satisfaction of the Secretary that all of the means referred to in paragraph (1) are not cost effective` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2022(b)(2) paragraph (1) does not apply` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the State agency has demonstrated to the satisfaction of the Secretary that all of the means referred to in paragraph (1) are not cost effective`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (1) shall not apply if the State agency demonstrates to the satisfaction of the Secretary"
            -- note (a failed "if"; see NOTES.md, Marginal readings)
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1815 | (3) Maximum reduction absent fraud
-- src:1816 | If a household received an overissuance of benefits without any member of the household being found ineligible to participate in the program under section 2015(b)(1) of this title and a State agency elects to reduce the allotment of the household under paragraph (1)(A), the State agency shall not reduce the monthly allotment of the household under paragraph (1)(A) by an amount in excess of the greater of—
-- src:1817 | (A) 10 percent of the monthly allotment of the household; or
-- src:1818 | (B) $10.
@ref s 2022(b)(3) the largest reduction of the allotment where no member is found ineligible for fraud (src:1815-1818)
-- In plain words: if no member of the household was found ineligible under section 2015(b)(1) and the State agency chooses to collect by cutting the monthly allotment, it may not cut it by more than the greater of 10 percent of the monthly allotment and $10.
GIVEN `a member of the household has been found ineligible to participate in the program under section 2015(b)(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency elects to reduce the allotment of the household under paragraph (1)(A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the monthly allotment of the household` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2022(b)(3) the greatest reduction of the monthly allotment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a member of the household has been found ineligible to participate in the program under section 2015(b)(1)` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without any member of the household being found ineligible to participate in the program under section 2015(b)(1) of this title"
            NOTHING
        IF `the State agency elects to reduce the allotment of the household under paragraph (1)(A)` THEN
            JUST (max (0.10 TIMES `the monthly allotment of the household`) 10)
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a State agency elects to reduce the allotment of the household under paragraph (1)(A)"
            NOTHING

-- src:1815 | (3) Maximum reduction absent fraud
-- src:1816 | If a household received an overissuance of benefits without any member of the household being found ineligible to participate in the program under section 2015(b)(1) of this title and a State agency elects to reduce the allotment of the household under paragraph (1)(A), the State agency shall not reduce the monthly allotment of the household under paragraph (1)(A) by an amount in excess of the greater of—
-- src:1817 | (A) 10 percent of the monthly allotment of the household; or
-- src:1818 | (B) $10.
@ref s 2022(b)(3) the State agency may reduce the monthly allotment by the amount (src:1815-1818)
GIVEN `a member of the household has been found ineligible to participate in the program under section 2015(b)(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency elects to reduce the allotment of the household under paragraph (1)(A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the monthly allotment of the household` IS A NUMBER
      `the reduction of the monthly allotment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2022(b)(3) the State agency may reduce the monthly allotment by the amount` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a member of the household has been found ineligible to participate in the program under section 2015(b)(1)` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without any member of the household being found ineligible to participate in the program under section 2015(b)(1) of this title"
            NOTHING
        IF NOT `the State agency elects to reduce the allotment of the household under paragraph (1)(A)` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a State agency elects to reduce the allotment of the household under paragraph (1)(A)"
            NOTHING
        IF `the reduction of the monthly allotment` GREATER THAN max (0.10 TIMES `the monthly allotment of the household`) 10 THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the State agency shall not reduce the monthly allotment of the household under paragraph (1)(A) by an amount in excess of the greater of"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- the reduction is within the cap, and paragraph (1)(A) lists reducing the allotment as a means of collection
            JUST TRUE

-- src:1819 | (4) Procedures
-- src:1820 | A State agency shall collect an overissuance of benefits issued to a household under paragraph (1) in accordance with the requirements established by the State agency for providing notice, electing a means of payment, and establishing a time schedule for payment.
@ref s 2022(b)(4) collection follows the requirements the State agency has set for notice, choice of payment and schedule (src:1819-1820)
GIVEN `the State agency gave notice in accordance with its requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household elected a means of payment in accordance with the State agency's requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a time schedule for payment was established in accordance with the State agency's requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2022(b)(4) the State agency collected the overissuance in accordance with its requirements` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency gave notice in accordance with its requirements` AND `the household elected a means of payment in accordance with the State agency's requirements` AND `a time schedule for payment was established in accordance with the State agency's requirements` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall collect an overissuance of benefits issued to a household under paragraph (1) in accordance with the requirements"
            -- note (a duty failed; see NOTES.md, Marginal readings)
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1821 | (5) Overissuances caused by systemic State errors
-- src:1822 | (A) In general
-- src:1823 | If the Secretary determines that a State agency overissued benefits to a substantial number of households in a fiscal year as a result of a major systemic error by the State agency, as defined by the Secretary, the Secretary may prohibit the State agency from collecting these overissuances from some or all households.
@ref s 2022(b)(5)(A) the Secretary may prohibit a State agency from collecting overissuances caused by its major systemic error (src:1821-1823)
-- In plain words: if the Secretary determines that a State agency overissued benefits to a substantial number of households in a fiscal year because of a major systemic error (as the Secretary defines it),
-- the Secretary may forbid that State agency to collect those overissuances from some or all households. Whether the State agency may then collect from a given household turns on the prohibition.
GIVEN `the Secretary has determined that the State agency overissued benefits to a substantial number of households in a fiscal year as a result of a major systemic error by the State agency` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary has prohibited the State agency from collecting the overissuance from the household` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2022(b)(5)(A) the State agency may collect the overissuance from the household` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary has prohibited the State agency from collecting the overissuance from the household` AND `the Secretary has determined that the State agency overissued benefits to a substantial number of households in a fiscal year as a result of a major systemic error by the State agency` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN
            -- the prohibition is the Secretary's power under this subparagraph and, exercised, forbids collection
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Secretary may prohibit the State agency from collecting these overissuances from some or all households"
            NOTHING

-- src:1825 | (i) Information reporting by States
-- src:1826 | Every State agency shall provide to the Secretary all information requested by the Secretary concerning the issuance of benefits to households by the State agency in the applicable fiscal year.
@ref s 2022(b)(5)(B)(i) every State agency shall give the Secretary the information requested (src:1825-1826)
GIVEN `the State agency provided to the Secretary all information requested by the Secretary concerning the issuance of benefits to households by the State agency in the applicable fiscal year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2022(b)(5)(B)(i) the State agency has provided the information requested` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency provided to the Secretary all information requested by the Secretary concerning the issuance of benefits to households by the State agency in the applicable fiscal year` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states no time by which the information must be provided
            NOTHING

-- src:1827 | (ii) Final determination
-- src:1828 | After reviewing relevant information provided by a State agency, the Secretary shall make a final determination—
-- src:1829 | (I) whether the State agency overissued benefits to a substantial number of households as a result of a systemic error in the applicable fiscal year; and
-- src:1830 | (II) as to the amount of the overissuance in the applicable fiscal year for which the State agency is liable.
@ref s 2022(b)(5)(B)(ii) the Secretary makes a final determination whether there was a systemic error and the amount for which the State agency is liable (src:1827-1830)
GIVEN `the Secretary has reviewed the relevant information provided by the State agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary has made a final determination whether the State agency overissued benefits to a substantial number of households as a result of a systemic error in the applicable fiscal year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary has made a final determination as to the amount of the overissuance in the applicable fiscal year for which the State agency is liable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2022(b)(5)(B)(ii) the Secretary has made the final determination` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary has reviewed the relevant information provided by the State agency` AND `the Secretary has made a final determination whether the State agency overissued benefits to a substantial number of households as a result of a systemic error in the applicable fiscal year` AND `the Secretary has made a final determination as to the amount of the overissuance in the applicable fiscal year for which the State agency is liable` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states no time by which the Secretary must make the final determination
            NOTHING

-- src:1831 | (iii) Establishing a claim
-- src:1832 | Upon determining under clause (ii) that a State agency has overissued benefits to households due to a major systemic error determined under subparagraph (A), the Secretary shall establish a claim against the State agency equal to the value of the overissuance caused by the systemic error.
@ref s 2022(b)(5)(B)(iii) the Secretary shall establish a claim against the State agency equal to the value of the overissuance caused by the systemic error (src:1831-1832)
GIVEN `the Secretary has determined under clause (ii) that the State agency has overissued benefits to households due to a major systemic error` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the overissuance caused by the systemic error` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE Claim
`s 2022(b)(5)(B)(iii) the claim against the State agency` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary has determined under clause (ii) that the State agency has overissued benefits to households due to a major systemic error` THEN
            JUST (Claim WITH `amount in dollars` IS `the value of the overissuance caused by the systemic error`, `owed by` IS `the State agency`, `owed to` IS `the Secretary`)
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Upon determining under clause (ii) that a State agency has overissued benefits to households due to a major systemic error"
            NOTHING

-- src:1833 | (iv) Administrative and judicial review
-- src:1834 | Administrative and judicial review, as provided in section 2023 of this title, shall apply to the final determinations by the Secretary under clause (ii).
@ref s 2022(b)(5)(B)(iv) administrative and judicial review under section 2023 applies to the Secretary's final determinations (src:1833-1834)
GIVEN `the determination is a final determination by the Secretary under clause (ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2022(b)(5)(B)(iv) administrative and judicial review under section 2023 applies to the determination` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the determination is a final determination by the Secretary under clause (ii)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the final determinations by the Secretary under clause (ii)"
            NOTHING

-- src:1835 | (v) Remission to the Secretary
-- src:1836 | (I) Determination not appealed
-- src:1837 | If the determination of the Secretary under clause (ii) is not appealed, the State agency shall, as soon as practicable, remit to the Secretary the dollar amount specified in the claim under clause (iii).
-- src:1838 | (II) Determination appealed
-- src:1839 | If the determination of the Secretary under clause (ii) is appealed, upon completion of administrative and judicial review under clause (iv), and a finding of liability on the part of the State, the appealing State agency shall, as soon as practicable, remit to the Secretary a dollar amount subject to the finding made in the administrative and judicial review.
@ref s 2022(b)(5)(B)(v) the State agency shall remit to the Secretary the amount of the claim (src:1835-1839)
-- In plain words: if the Secretary's determination is not appealed, the State agency remits the whole claim as soon as practicable; if it is appealed, after administrative and judicial review and a finding of liability it remits the amount that finding supports.
-- No date is stated ("as soon as practicable").
GIVEN `the determination of the Secretary under clause (ii) is appealed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `administrative and judicial review under clause (iv) is complete` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a finding of liability on the part of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dollar amount specified in the claim under clause (iii)` IS A NUMBER
      `the dollar amount subject to the finding made in the administrative and judicial review` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2022(b)(5)(B)(v) the dollar amount the State agency must remit to the Secretary` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the determination of the Secretary under clause (ii) is appealed` THEN JUST `the dollar amount specified in the claim under clause (iii)`
        IF `administrative and judicial review under clause (iv) is complete` AND `there is a finding of liability on the part of the State` THEN JUST `the dollar amount subject to the finding made in the administrative and judicial review`
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "upon completion of administrative and judicial review under clause (iv), and a finding of liability on the part of the State"
            NOTHING

-- src:1840 | (vi) Alternative method of collection
-- src:1841 | (I) In general
-- src:1842 | If a State agency fails to make a payment under clause (v) within a reasonable period of time, as determined by the Secretary, the Secretary may reduce any amount due to the State agency under any other provision of this chapter by the amount due.
-- src:1843 | (II) Accrual of interest
-- src:1844 | During the period of time determined by the Secretary to be reasonable under subclause (I), interest in the amount owed shall not accrue.
@ref s 2022(b)(5)(B)(vi)(I) the Secretary may reduce amounts due to the State agency when it fails to pay within a reasonable period (src:1840-1844)
GIVEN `the State agency failed to make a payment under clause (v) within a reasonable period of time, as determined by the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2022(b)(5)(B)(vi)(I) the Secretary may reduce any amount due to the State agency by the amount due` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency failed to make a payment under clause (v) within a reasonable period of time, as determined by the Secretary` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a State agency fails to make a payment under clause (v) within a reasonable period of time, as determined by the Secretary"
            NOTHING

-- src:1840 | (vi) Alternative method of collection
-- src:1841 | (I) In general
-- src:1842 | If a State agency fails to make a payment under clause (v) within a reasonable period of time, as determined by the Secretary, the Secretary may reduce any amount due to the State agency under any other provision of this chapter by the amount due.
-- src:1843 | (II) Accrual of interest
-- src:1844 | During the period of time determined by the Secretary to be reasonable under subclause (I), interest in the amount owed shall not accrue.
@ref s 2022(b)(5)(B)(vi)(II) interest in the amount owed does not accrue during the reasonable period (src:1840-1844)
GIVEN `the time is within the period determined by the Secretary to be reasonable under subclause (I)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2022(b)(5)(B)(vi)(II) interest in the amount owed accrues` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the time is within the period determined by the Secretary to be reasonable under subclause (I)` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "interest in the amount owed shall not accrue"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "During the period of time determined by the Secretary to be reasonable under subclause (I)"
            NOTHING

-- src:1845 | (vii) Limitation
-- src:1846 | Any liability amount established under section 2025(c)(1)(C) of this title shall be reduced by the amount of the claim established under this subparagraph.
@ref s 2022(b)(5)(B)(vii) any liability amount established under section 2025(c)(1)(C) is reduced by the amount of the claim (src:1845-1846)
GIVEN `the liability amount established under section 2025(c)(1)(C)` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the claim established under this subparagraph` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2022(b)(5)(B)(vii) the liability amount after the reduction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the amount of the claim established under this subparagraph` GREATER THAN `the liability amount established under section 2025(c)(1)(C)` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say what happens when the claim is larger than the liability amount
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the liability amount established under section 2025(c)(1)(C)` MINUS `the amount of the claim established under this subparagraph`)

§§ `s 2022(c) intercept of unemployment benefits`

-- src:1847 | (c) Intercept of unemployment benefits
-- src:1848 | (1) As used in this subsection, the term “uncollected overissuance” means the amount of an overissuance of benefits, as determined under subsection (b)(1), that has not been recovered pursuant to subsection (b)(1).
@ref s 2022(c)(1) uncollected overissuance (src:1847-1848)
-- In plain words: the uncollected overissuance is the amount of the overissuance, worked out under subsection (b)(1), that has not been recovered; recovered in full means nothing is uncollected.
GIVEN `the amount of an overissuance of benefits, as determined under subsection (b)(1)` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount recovered pursuant to subsection (b)(1)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2022(c)(1) the uncollected overissuance` MEANS
    max 0 (`the amount of an overissuance of benefits, as determined under subsection (b)(1)` MINUS `the amount recovered pursuant to subsection (b)(1)`)

-- src:1849 | (2) A State agency may determine on a periodic basis, from information supplied pursuant to section 49b(b) of title 29, whether an individual receiving compensation under the State’s unemployment compensation law (including amounts payable pursuant to an agreement under a Federal unemployment compensation law) owes an uncollected overissuance.
@ref s 2022(c)(2) the State agency may determine from information supplied under section 49b(b) of title 29 whether an individual receiving unemployment compensation owes an uncollected overissuance (src:1849)
GIVEN `the individual is receiving compensation under the State's unemployment compensation law, including amounts payable pursuant to an agreement under a Federal unemployment compensation law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2022(c)(2) the State agency may determine on a periodic basis whether the individual owes an uncollected overissuance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the individual is receiving compensation under the State's unemployment compensation law, including amounts payable pursuant to an agreement under a Federal unemployment compensation law` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an individual receiving compensation under the State’s unemployment compensation law"
            NOTHING

-- src:1850 | (3) A State agency may recover an uncollected overissuance—
-- src:1851 | (A) by—
-- src:1852 | (i) entering into an agreement with an individual described in paragraph (2) under which specified amounts will be withheld from unemployment compensation otherwise payable to the individual; and
-- src:1853 | (ii) furnishing a copy of the agreement to the State agency administering the unemployment compensation law; or
-- src:1854 | (B) in the absence of an agreement, by obtaining a writ, order, summons, or other similar process in the nature of garnishment from a court of competent jurisdiction to require the withholding of amounts from the unemployment compensation.
@ref s 2022(c)(3) the State agency may recover an uncollected overissuance from unemployment compensation (src:1850-1854)
-- In plain words: either by an agreement with the individual under which amounts are withheld from the compensation, with a copy given to the agency that pays it,
-- or, if there is no agreement, by getting a court's writ, order, summons or similar process in the nature of garnishment.
GIVEN `the individual is one described in paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an agreement under which specified amounts will be withheld from unemployment compensation otherwise payable to the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the agreement has been furnished to the State agency administering the unemployment compensation law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency has obtained a writ, order, summons, or other similar process in the nature of garnishment from a court of competent jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2022(c)(3) the State agency may recover the uncollected overissuance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the individual is one described in paragraph (2)` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an agreement with an individual described in paragraph (2)"
            NOTHING
        IF `there is an agreement under which specified amounts will be withheld from unemployment compensation otherwise payable to the individual` AND `a copy of the agreement has been furnished to the State agency administering the unemployment compensation law` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (NOT `there is an agreement under which specified amounts will be withheld from unemployment compensation otherwise payable to the individual`) AND `the State agency has obtained a writ, order, summons, or other similar process in the nature of garnishment from a court of competent jurisdiction` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names two routes and does not say that no other route exists
            NOTHING

§§ `s 2022(d) recovery of overissuance of benefits`

-- src:1855 | (d) Recovery of overissuance of benefits
-- src:1856 | The amount of an overissuance of benefits, as determined under subsection (b)(1), that has not been recovered pursuant to such subsection may be recovered from Federal pay (including salaries and pensions) as authorized by section 5514 of title 5 or a Federal income tax refund as authorized by section 3720A of title 31.
@ref s 2022(d) an uncollected overissuance may be recovered from Federal pay or a Federal income tax refund (src:1855-1856)
GIVEN `the amount of the overissuance, as determined under subsection (b)(1), that has not been recovered pursuant to that subsection` IS A NUMBER
      `the source` IS A `s 2022(d) source of recovery`
      `the recovery is as authorized by section 5514 of title 5 or section 3720A of title 31` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2022(d) the uncollected overissuance may be recovered from the source` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the amount of the overissuance, as determined under subsection (b)(1), that has not been recovered pursuant to that subsection` AT MOST 0 THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): nothing is left to recover
            NOTHING
        IF `the source` EQUALS `s 2022(d) any other source` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may be recovered from Federal pay (including salaries and pensions) as authorized by section 5514 of title 5 or a Federal income tax refund as authorized by section 3720A of title 31"
            NOTHING
        IF `the recovery is as authorized by section 5514 of title 5 or section 3720A of title 31` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the recovery is authorized by section 5514 of title 5 or section 3720A of title 31 is decided by those sections
            NOTHING
